# Performance

This package must be fast as well as correct. Optimize **computation**: work per observation and per horizon step. Follow [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).

## Do

- Fit in one **O(n)** pass over training values (SES, Holt, mean, drift)
- Reduce the fitted model to the state `Forecast` needs (last, step, level/trend, season); do not keep the full series
- Fill the horizon in one **O(h)** loop; `at(k)` must be O(1)
- Copy `Times()` / `Values()` once in `prepare`; compute on those slices
- Score metrics in one pass over aligned values
- Add or update `bench_test.go` when changing a fit or `Forecast` hot path

## Do not

- Re-scan training values inside `Forecast(h)` or per horizon step
- Nested O(n²) loops over observations (including seasonal)
- Re-fit on every `Forecast` call
- Clone the training series unless a public helper needs an independent copy
- Add SIMD, GPU, or a parallel API without updating INTENTIONS
